# The unattended system prompt must be BYTE-IDENTICAL to what Anthropic published.
# Without this, autocrlf rewrites its line endings on checkout, and a Linux clone
# and a Windows clone hold different bytes under the same "verbatim" claim -- while
# the test that checks it passes on both, because both copies got converted.
#
# This is the same mechanism that would have broken every SHA-256 in every
# provenance.json in Stasis-Catacomb had it not been caught there.
prompts/*.txt -text

# VBScript is parsed by wscript.exe on Windows only; leave it alone too.
*.vbs -text
